    "consumed_by_exp_id": "",
    "description": "# Future directions\n\nThe new file `Catalog/Applications/SurveillanceNetworks/PrivacyThreshold.lean`\nsettles the \"sharp privacy threshold\" direction for binary network histories:\nperfectly private channels \u2014 deterministic or randomized \u2014 achieve worst-case\nHamming distortion `D` exactly when a single ball of radius `D` covers the\nhistory space, so the optimal private distortion is the covering radius of the\none-codeword code, and for binary tensors this is the full ambient dimension\n`T\u00b7n\u00b2`. On the quantitative side the Hamming ball volume is computed exactly,\nturning the fibre-covering converse into `2^{T n\u00b2} \u2264 rate \u00b7 \u2211_{i \u2264 D} C(T n\u00b2, i)`,\nwith an excess-distortion version where only a good set of histories must be\nreconstructed.\n\nOpen follow-ups:\n\n1. **Entropy-sensitive converse.** Replace the counting version of the excess\n   set by a probability measure: for a source law `p` on histories and a channel\n   with excess-distortion probability `\u03b5`, prove\n   `H(X) - H(X | Y) \u2265 H(X) - log(vol_D) - h(\u03b5) - \u03b5\u00b7log|S|` (Fano-type\n   correction). The combinatorial skeleton (`card_good_le_rate_mul_ball`) is the\n   counting shadow of this statement.\n\n2. **Average- rather than worst-case distortion.** The threshold theorems here\n   use almost-sure distortion. Under expected distortion a private channel can\n   do better than the covering radius; identify the exact private\n   rate\u2013distortion function `D_priv(p) = min_c E_p[d(c, X)]` and compare it to\n   the covering radius.\n\n3. **Causal / sequential covering.** For time-indexed histories the record is\n   produced online; replace the single covering number by a sequential covering\n   number along the natural filtration and relate the resulting quantity to\n   directed information.\n\n4. **Structured sources.** For histories generated by a Markov chain on\n   snapshots, the ambient count `2^{T n\u00b2}` is far from tight; a mixing-based\n   deficit in the exponent is the natural next quantitative target.\n\n5. **Distortion modulo relabeling.** Replace Hamming balls by orbit balls under\n   the `S_n` action on vertices; the exact volume computation\n   (`hamming_ball_card`) must be replaced by an orbit-counting (Burnside) volume,\n   with graph asymmetry controlling the loss.\n",
