    "description": "# Future Directions\n\nConjectures suggested by the formalization in `Catalog/Bridges/VertexSplitting.lean` and\n`Catalog/Bridges/VertexSplittingExact.lean`.\nAll are stated in the vocabulary of those files (`IsSplit`, `IsExclusive`, `IsProjExclusive`,\n`SplitChain`, `IsCograph`, `IsChordal`, `IsPtFree`, `HasUnitIntervalRep`, `HasInducedClaw`,\n`matchingGraph`, `starGraph`).\n\nThroughout, `split_\u03a0(G)` denotes the minimum of `|W| \u2212 |V|` over all `H : SimpleGraph W`\nand `f : W \u2192 V` with `IsSplit G H f` and `\u03a0 H`.\n\n## Resolved in this project\n\n* Every splitting map factors into single `singleSplit` steps, and the factorization can be taken\n  shallow: `exists_singleSplit_factor`, `SplitChain.of_isSplit`, `splitChain_matchingGraph`.\n  Consequently, in this model shallowness costs nothing.\n* Unit interval graphs are chordal: `isChordal_of_unitIntervalRep`.  Hence\n  `split_IsChordal(G) \u2264 split_HasUnitIntervalRep(G)` for every `G`.\n* Exact splitting numbers of the smallest obstructions:\n  `split_IsCograph(P\u2084) = 1` (`cograph_split_pathP4_exact`),\n  `split_IsChordal(C\u2084) = 1` (`chordal_split_cycleC4_exact`),\n  `split_HasUnitIntervalRep(K_{1,3}) = split_HasUnitIntervalRep(K_{1,4}) = 1`\n  (`unitInterval_split_starK13_exact`, `unitInterval_split_starK14_exact`).\n  In each case the optimal split can be taken exclusive.\n* **A conjecture of the previous iteration was refuted.**  It was conjectured that\n  `split_HasUnitIntervalRep(K_{1,n}) = n \u2212 2`.  In fact pairing up the leaves gives\n  `split_HasUnitIntervalRep(K_{1,n}) = \u2308n/2\u2309 \u2212 1` for every `n \u2265 1`\n  (`unitInterval_split_star_exact`), with a matching lower bound valid for every claw-free target\n  (`card_ge_of_split_clawFree_star`).  For `n = 4` the true value is `1`, not `2`.\n\n## Conjectures\n\n1. **Exclusive splittings need not decompose into exclusive single splits.**\n   `SplitChain.of_isSplit` produces an *exclusive* chain (each `singleSplit` step has\n   `A \u2229 B = \u2205`) from the hypothesis `IsProjExclusive H f`, which is strictly stronger than\n   `IsExclusive H f`.  Conjecture: there are finite `G, H, f` with `IsSplit G H f` and\n   `IsExclusive H f` for which **no** chain `SplitChain True G H f` exists \u2014 i.e. the ordering\n   of splits genuinely matters for exclusivity, and `IsProjExclusive` is the right invariant.\n   Falsifiable by proving `IsExclusive H f \u2192 SplitChain True G H f` in general.\n\n2. **No exclusivity gap for cograph splitting.**\n   (Exclusivity is automatic when the target has maximum degree at most one \u2014\n   `isExclusive_of_deg_le_one` \u2014 and all optimal splits computed in this project are exclusive.)\n   For every finite graph `G`, the minimum number of splits producing a cograph equals the\n   minimum number of *exclusive* splits producing a cograph.\n   Falsifiable by a graph whose exclusive cograph splitting number is strictly larger than its\n   unrestricted one.\n\n3. **A cyclomatic bound for chordal targets.**\n   For every finite `G`, `split_IsChordal(G) \u2264 |E| \u2212 |V| + c(G)`, where `c(G)` is the number of\n   connected components; i.e. one split per independent cycle suffices.  The case of a single\n   cycle is proved for `C\u2084` (`chordal_split_cycleC4_exact`), where unfolding the cycle at one\n   vertex produces the path `P\u2085` (`isSplit_pathP5_cycleC4`).  Falsifiable by a graph needing more\n   splits than its cyclomatic number.\n\n4. **A local degree lower bound for claw-free (hence unit interval) targets.**\n   For every finite `G`, every splitting of `G` into a claw-free graph has at least\n   `\u03a3_v \u2308deg(v)/2\u2309` vertices coming from vertices of degree at least one, so\n   `split_HasUnitIntervalRep(G) \u2265 \u03a3_v (\u2308deg(v)/2\u2309 \u2212 1)`.\n   This is exactly `card_ge_of_split_clawFree_star` when `G` is a star, where it is tight.\n   Falsifiable by a graph and a claw-free splitting violating the count.\n\n5. **Hereditary monotonicity under induced subgraphs.**\n   If `\u03a0` is hereditary (closed under induced subgraphs) then `split_\u03a0(G') \u2264 split_\u03a0(G)` for\n   every induced subgraph `G'` of `G`; in particular this holds for `IsCograph`, `IsPtFree t`,\n   `IsChordal` and `HasUnitIntervalRep`.  Falsifiable by an induced subgraph that needs strictly\n   more splits than the whole graph, for one of these classes.\n",
